course: dictionary
lesson: 11634
title: Words from music: aria
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An aria is a song that one singer performs alone. It usually happens in an opera, a play where the actors sing most of the words, often with an orchestra playing.
explain: Look for the context clues. «The singer stepped into the spotlight and sang an aria, alone on the stage.» One singer, alone, singing: that tells you an aria is a song for one voice. Try the swap test: put "a song for one singer" in place of aria, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: An aria is often slow and full of feeling. It shows what a character is feeling at that moment. «The hero's aria made the whole audience go quiet.» The song was so moving that the audience was silent, so the aria must have been very emotional.
fact: An aria is a song for one singer.
fact: An aria is usually found in an opera.
fact: Arias are often sung by a soprano or a tenor, and they show what a character feels.
fact: «Aria» can also mean a slow, tuneful piece of music, like that kind of song.
fact: Aria is also a girl's name, so the sentence tells you which meaning is used.
exercise: «The singer stepped onto the stage and sang an aria alone.» What is an aria here? | A type of stage light | A group of dancers | *A song for one singer | A loud drum
exercise: «The opera ended with a long, sad aria.» What does aria mean in this sentence? | *A long, sad song for one singer | A short joke | A fast dance
exercise: Which sentence uses aria as a girl's name? | «The aria was sung by a tenor on the stage.» | «The aria moved the whole audience to tears.» | *«Aria waved to me from the back of the class.»
test: «The tenor's aria showed that the hero was heartbroken.» What does the aria show? | The weather outside | *The hero's feelings | The price of the tickets | The seats in the theatre
test: Which of these is the best description of an aria? | Loud shouting in a crowd | *A song for one singer, often full of feeling | A kind of painting | A quick race on foot
exam: Read this: «The soprano stepped forward and began her aria.» What does aria mean here? | A dance | *A song for one singer | A stage curtain | A ticket
